  "validity_note": "CoolProp's incompressible aqueous methanol correlation (INCOMP::MMA), built on Melinder (2010). Tabulated for 10-50 wt% methanol over -45 to 40 degC. Methanol is a non-electrolyte freeze-protection brine, so it is modelled with CoolProp rather than the Laliberte electrolyte correlation. Each cell sits above the solution's freezing line at that strength: cells below it (where the solution is no longer liquid) are left blank rather than tabulated, and the explorer will not interpolate across them. Methanol is volatile and flammable, so closed handling is assumed. Values are for preliminary design; verify against vendor data for critical service.",
